      "description": "NDSU Jobs Skip to main content North Dakota State University cta Apply Visit Request Info Search Toggle Main Navigation main Academics Academics Menu Study at NDSU Study at NDSU Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Accelerated Programs Colleges Colleges Menu Agriculture, Food Systems, and Natural Resources Arts and Sciences Business Engineering Health and Human Sciences Graduate School Back to level 1 Admission & Cost Admission & Cost Menu Admission Admission Cost & Aid Visit Admitted Students Graduate Admission For Parents & Families For Counselors & Advisors Contact Back to level 1 Bison Life Bison Life Menu Bison Life Bison Life Housing & Dining Services for Student Success Organizations & Engagement Experiential Learning Arts & Culture Events Back to level 1 About About Menu About About The Campus Fargo & the Community Alumni News Industry Relations Bison Youth (PreK-12) Contact Back to level 1 Research Research Menu Research Impact Research & Creative Activity Extension Back to level 1 Athletics Utility Current Students Faculty & Staff One Stop Jobs Give Directory A-Z Index Close Main Navigation NDSU Jobs Employment Opportunities Applicants : When creating an account or logging into your account, please use Microsoft Edge browser for the best experience. External Candidates New Applicants will be prompted to “Register Now.” If you have previously applied to a position, login using your username and password before applying. Note – any changes you make to your new application will not update any applications you have already submitted. If you encounter any technical issues when applying for a job, please click: submit ticket online. External Candidates Current Employees Employees at NDSU or ND University Institutions: Log in to Employee Self-Service and navigate to the “Careers” tile to view all internal & external postings. Current Employees Student Employment This link will take you to Career Services - Handshake Job Posting site. Student Employment For our benefited employee, NDSU offers 100% employer-paid health insurance premium, along with tuition benefits and competitive retirement plans. For more detailed information on NDSU Benefits - Benefits NDSU is an R1 research institution as defined by the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education. R1 is the top Carnegie status and is presented to only the top research institutions in the country that have a high level of research expenditures and produce PhD graduates across a balanced portfolio of disciplines. To request an accommodation to complete an application, please email ndsu.jobs@ndsu.edu . Employment Information Tobacco/Nicotine - Free Facilities NDSU is a Tobacco/Nicotine - Free Facility in accordance with N.D.C.C. § 23-12-10 Tobacco/Nicotine - Free Facilities Policy (pdf) Annual Safety Report NDSU is committed to assisting all members of the campus community in providing for their own personal safety and security. Information regarding campus security, personal safety and security and fire safety, including topics such as crime prevention, university police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, crime statistics for the most current three year period, and disciplinary procedures is included in the Annual Security and Fire Report . Pre-Employment Screening Unless otherwise noted, all NDSU employees are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a review of criminal records and reference checks. NDSU determines employment eligibility through the E-Verify system. E-Verify Poster Veterans claiming preference must submit all proof of eligibility by the closing date. Proof of eligibility includes a DD-214, NGB 22 and if claiming disabled status, a copy of a VA statement dated within the past year. Veterans claiming preference must submit all proof of eligibility by the closing date of application. Non-Discrimination Policy NDSU is an EEO employer and does not discriminate in its programs and activities on the basis of age, color, gender expression/identity, genetic information, marital status, national origin, participation in lawful off-campus activity, physical or mental disability, pregnancy, public assistance status, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, spousal relationship to current employee, or veteran status, as applicable. Direct inquiries to Vice Provost, Title IX/ADA Coordinator , Old Main 201, (701) 231-7708, ndsu.eoaa@ndsu.edu . Related Links Campus Map Explore Fargo Employment Email: ndsu.hr@ndsu.edu Phone: (701) 231-8961 Page Manager North Dakota State University Fargo, N.D. North Dakota State University Footer A-Z Index Campus Map Consumer Information Contact One Stop Quick Links Social Navigation facebook instagram linkedin twitter youtube ©2026 North Dakota State University Privacy Statement | Nondiscrimination Statement NDSU Web | Website and Accessibility Feedback"
